{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CfpkBPatkSXUDku5Q6PiV","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"As far as I know, Cloudflare Workflows has **no per-workflow \"max concurrency\" setting** in `wrangler.toml`/`wrangler.jsonc`. The only cap is the platform's account-level concurrent-instance limit, and instances created beyond it simply wait in a `queued` state. Check the current Workflows \"Limits\" docs, since this may have changed.\n\nTo enforce your own lower cap, gate instance creation yourself:\n\n- **Queue:** Push jobs to a Cloudflare Queue and have the consumer call `env.MY_WORKFLOW.create()`, using the consumer's `max_concurrency` to throttle it.\n- **Durable Object semaphore:** Have a Durable Object count running instances. Each instance acquires a slot in its first `step.do()` and releases it in its last step.\n\nThe Durable Object approach caps instances that are actually running, while the Queue approach only limits how fast new instances are created."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2247,"cache_read_input_tokens":535,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2247},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"dd76be11-37d6-4d91-bee3-7d688c5c8db2","uuid":"443ad3d9-bfe4-4268-a301-aeb93814f740","timestamp":"2026-10-08T12:09:42.143Z","request_id":"req_011CfpkBPC5T3hVwnKvim6JE"}
